## 8. Envelope Consistency (B10)

### The problem

- Backend: `utils/response.js` → `{ success, data, meta }` for success and
  `utils/apiError.js` → `{ success:false, error:{code,message,status,requestId} }`
  for errors. Consistent.
- BUT `controllers/adsController.js` called `res.json({ads, session})` (6
  sites) — those responses did NOT have the `{success, data, meta}` wrapper.
  So the ads API returned a different shape than every other endpoint.

### The fix

All 6 success paths in `adsController.js` now use `sendSuccess(res, payload, meta)`:

| Before                                      | After                                           |
| ------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| `res.json({ success: true, ads, session })` | `sendSuccess(res, { ads, session, isPremium })` |
| `res.json({ config })`                      | `sendSuccess(res, config)`                      |
| `res.json({ ads: [], session: null })`      | `sendSuccess(res, { ads: [], session: null })`  |

`sendSuccess` always produces `{ success: true, data: payload, meta: {} }`.
Error responses were not touched (they already used `sendError`/`ApiError`).

Every `/api/*` endpoint now returns a uniform envelope. No client needs a
special case for ads.

