## 11. Environment Variables

### .env.example (authoritative list — copy to real `.env` and Render dashboard)

| variable                     | purpose                                         | example                                         |
| ---------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| `API_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`        | Extra web origins allowed in dev                | `https://anistrim.com,https://www.anistrim.com` |
| `DESKTOP_ORIGINS`            | Electron custom schemes (prod)                  | `app://anistrim-desktop`                        |
| `SERVE_WEB`                  | Mount Web/ static root (bool)                   | `true`                                          |
| `WEB_DIR`                    | Web directory                                   | `Web`                                           |
| `WEB_MOUNT_PATH`             | URL prefix for Web client                       | `/web`                                          |
| `SERVE_DESKTOP_PREVIEW`      | Mount Desktop/ at /desktop-preview              | `false`                                         |
| `DESKTOP_DIR`                | Desktop directory                               | `Desktop`                                       |
| `PRIMARY_HOST_WEB`           | Host header → serve Web at /                    | (empty = both share /)                          |
| `PRIMARY_HOST_MOBILE`        | Host header → serve Frontend at /               | (empty = both share /)                          |
| `RESET_PATHS_JSON`           | Per-client reset paths allow-list               | `{"mobile":"reset","web":"reset"}`              |
| `GOOGLE_RETURN_TARGETS_JSON` | Per-client Google deep-link targets             | `{"mobile":"anistrim://auth"}`                  |
| `FRONTEND_URL`               | Base URL for frontend (used in forgot-password) | `https://anistrim.com`                          |
| `BACKEND_URL`                | This server's URL                               | `https://anistrimbackend.onrender.com`          |
| `JWT_SECRET`                 | (existing)                                      | —                                               |

**Capacitor origins** (`capacitor://localhost`, `https://localhost`, etc.)
are ALWAYS allowed and do NOT need to be in `API_ALLOWED_ORIGINS`.

